---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="PairPilotFX Privacy Policy, including Google and YouTube API data handling."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="policy">
    <p class="eyebrow">PairPilotFX</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how PairPilotFX handles information in connection with its website,
      internal publishing automation, and Google/YouTube authorization.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX does not currently offer public user accounts through this website. We may receive
      information that you voluntarily provide when contacting us by email.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our private publishing system uses Google OAuth to connect to the PairPilot FX YouTube channel.
      For that integration, the application requests:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>YouTube read-only access</strong> to identify and validate the connected YouTube channel.</li>
      <li><strong>YouTube upload access</strong> to upload PairPilotFX-created videos and Shorts to that channel.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX does not request access to Gmail, Google Drive, contacts, calendars, passwords,
      payment information, or unrelated Google Account data through this integration.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How Google and YouTube data is used</h2>
    <p>
      Google/YouTube authorization data is used only to operate the PairPilotFX publishing workflow,
      confirm the connected channel, and upload PairPilotFX-created video content.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell Google user data, use it for advertising, or use it to build advertising profiles.
      We do not transfer Google user data to third parties except when necessary to operate the service,
      comply with law, protect rights or security, or when expressly authorized by the account holder.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX handles information obtained through Google APIs in accordance with the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google API Services User Data Policy
      </a>, including its Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>4. OAuth credentials and security</h2>
    <p>
      OAuth access and refresh credentials used by the PairPilotFX publishing system are stored on
      PairPilotFX-controlled infrastructure and are used only by the publishing service. We apply
      reasonable technical and organizational safeguards intended to prevent unauthorized access,
      disclosure, alteration, or loss.
    </p>
    <p>
      No internet-connected system can be guaranteed to be completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
      absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      OAuth credentials are retained while the YouTube integration remains connected and operational.
      Operational logs and publishing records may be retained as needed for reliability, auditability,
      troubleshooting, and security. Website attribution held in browser session storage is scoped to the
      active browser session. If analytics events are collected by a configured reporting endpoint, they
      may be retained as needed for aggregate product and funnel analysis. We aim to avoid storing unnecessary
      Google user data or unnecessary website visitor data.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Revoking Google access</h2>
    <p>
      Access can be revoked at any time from the Google Account's third-party connections or security
      settings. Revoking access prevents PairPilotFX from using the affected Google/YouTube authorization
      until authorization is completed again.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also contact us at
      <a href="mailto:pairpilotfx@gmail.com">pairpilotfx@gmail.com</a>
      to request disconnection or deletion of OAuth credentials held by PairPilotFX.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Website analytics and technical data</h2>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX uses first-party website instrumentation to understand page usage, campaign attribution,
      and interactions with links such as Weekly Brief, Substack, methodology, and Radar calls to action.
      The site may store an anonymous browser-session identifier and UTM campaign parameters in
      <code>sessionStorage</code> for the active browser session. This instrumentation does not use
      advertising cookies or create a persistent advertising profile.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics events are designed to contain only information needed for aggregate funnel measurement,
      such as the page path and title, referring hostname, UTM campaign fields, anonymous session identifier,
      event name, CTA placement, and destination. PairPilotFX does not intentionally include names, email
      addresses, form contents, passwords, or full referring URLs in this event payload.
    </p>
    <p>
      When an analytics collection endpoint is configured, these events may be transmitted to
      PairPilotFX-controlled or contracted infrastructure for aggregate reporting. Hosting, network,
      security, or analytics infrastructure may also process technical information such as IP addresses,
      request timestamps, browser information, or server logs as necessary to deliver and protect the service.
      PairPilotFX does not use this website analytics instrumentation for personalized advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      The PairPilot Trade Preparation Checklist stores its working state locally in the visitor's browser.
      Instrument labels, checklist selections, and preparation notes entered into the tool are not intentionally
      included in PairPilotFX analytics events. Tool analytics may record aggregate interaction metadata such as
      opening the tool, completing all checklist conditions, or resetting the checklist.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX services are not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children through this website or the YouTube publishing integration.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy as PairPilotFX evolves. The “Last updated” date above will be
      changed when material revisions are published.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, Google/YouTube authorization questions, or deletion requests, contact
      <a href="mailto:pairpilotfx@gmail.com">pairpilotfx@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
